#: ../../../badges.rst:2
msgid "Status badges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:4
msgid ""
"Status badges let you show the state of your documentation to your users. "
"They will show if the latest build has passed, failed, or is in an unknown "
"state. They are great for embedding in your README, or putting inside your "
"actual doc pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:9
msgid "You can see a badge in action in the `Read the Docs README`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:12
msgid "Display states"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:14
msgid "Badges have the following states which can be shown to users:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:16
msgid "**Green**: ``passing`` - the last build was successful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:17
msgid "**Red**: ``failing`` - the last build failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Yellow**: ``unknown`` - we couldn't figure out the status of your last "
"build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:20
msgid "An example of each is shown here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:22
msgid "|green| |nbsp| |red| |nbsp| |yellow|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:107
msgid "green"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:108
msgid "red"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:109
msgid "yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:25
msgid "Automatically generated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:27
msgid ""
"Badges are generated on-demand for all Read the Docs projects, using the "
"following URL syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:29
msgid ""
"https://app.readthedocs.org/projects/<project-slug>/badge/?"
"version=<version>&style=<style>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:34 ../../../badges.rst:41
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../badges.rst:36
msgid ""
"You can pass the ``style`` GET argument to get custom styled badges. This "
"allows you to match the look and feel of your website. By default, the "
"``flat`` style is used."
msgstr ""

